Stop conditions, which are outcomes and not failures:

- Anything `CLAUDE.md` → *When to wait* covers. Report which one and leave the PR open.
- A `manual — ` work order you cannot finish and verify — an upgrade plan, a DB format
  migration, release notes naming a breaking change.
- A PR whose new version you cannot verify actually took effect after landing.
- A PR whose title OR BRANCH carries `k8s_autodeploy: false`, wherever in the parenthetical it
  sits — the denylist rule leads with it, and a per-package rule ends with it after its own work
  order (the crowdsec bouncer plugin, meilisearch, karakeep's time-tagger deps, n8n). Read both
  with one call, `gh pr list --author app/renovate --json number,title,headRefName`: Renovate
  drops the group name from the title of a group holding ONE dependency and titles it `Update
  <dep> …` instead, so for some of these PRs the marker survives only in the branch, slugified
  as `k8s_autodeploy-false` (#2641). #2620 was a denied role's pin titled `Update
  klutchell/unbound Docker tag to v1.26.1`, and its branch is what named it. Every rule
  carrying the marker sets `groupSingleUpdates: true` since #2646 and #2654, so newer PRs carry
  the marker in the title as well; a PR raised before that can still title bare,
  which is why the branch stays the tell you must read. That phrase
  is not a work order for you, and neither is the one in front of it: it marks a role whose
  failed deploy the health gate cannot see (authelia's middleware answers before the backend,
  traefik's outage leaves the host probes green), so the review its denial asks for is a
  person, and your gated land is not that person. Do not merge it, do not land it. Name it in the summary with the command an interactive session
  runs: `./scripts/deploy_tools/land.sh --pr <n> --since <sha> --arm-merge --await-merge`,
  where `<sha>` is `origin/master` at the moment that session merges — leave it as the
  placeholder, since any SHA you write now is stale by then.

A `manual — ` work order you finish ends as a superseding PR you opened, which is not
Renovate's, so `land.sh --arm-merge` refuses it under `LAND_REQUIRE_AUTHOR`. That is the
operator's decision (#2746), not an obstacle to work around: never pass `--any-author`. Leave
that PR open and file a hand-off finding for it as the skill's §4 describes: what you
verified, its `land.sh --pr <n>` command with `<sha>` as the placeholder, the check that
proves the new version took effect, and that it must land before the next Renovate PR for
the same pin. Push that PR from a branch named `{{ renovate_agent_branch }}-<renovate pr number>`,
cut in this worktree with `git switch -c` before your first commit. The wrapper finds the PRs
you handed off by that name for the digest, and a PR pushed from `{{ renovate_agent_branch }}`
itself blocks every later tick until a person lands it.

For every other PR you leave open for a reason other than "ran out of budget" or the
`k8s_autodeploy: false` rule above, file a finding:
`uv run python scripts/dev/findings.py open --title … --body-file … --severity … --kind …`.
An unfiled reason reaches nobody — this session's transcript is read only when the digest
already says something went wrong. A `k8s_autodeploy: false` PR is meant to sit open until
a person lands it, so its handoff is the digest line, never a finding re-filed every morning.

